quiz.prompt:
The encoder is connected with CLK=D2, DT=D3, and sayac starts at 5. The encoder is turned 2 ticks in the opposite direction (each tick goes through the states 11, 10, 00, 01, 11). In the end, what does the last line on the Serial monitor say?

```
volatile int sayac = 5;

void adim() {
  if (digitalRead(3) == HIGH) {
    sayac++;
  } else {
    sayac--;
  }
}
// setup: attachInterrupt(digitalPinToInterrupt(2), adim, FALLING);
// loop: when sayac changes, prints Serial.print("Sayac: ") and the value
```

You connected the CLK wire to D4, and the program does not count or give a direction. The counter never changes. Which line is wrong?

```
const int CLK = 4;
const int DT = 3;
volatile int sayac = 0;

void adim() {
  if (digitalRead(DT) == HIGH) sayac++; else sayac--;
}

void setup() {
  pinMode(CLK, INPUT_PULLUP);
  pinMode(DT, INPUT_PULLUP);
  attachInterrupt(digitalPinToInterrupt(CLK), adim, FALLING);
}
```
